  "question": {
    "text": "Two coherent monochromatic light beams of intensities 4I and 9I are superimposed. The difference between the maximum and minimum intensities in the resulting interference pattern is xI. The value of $x$ is ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "24",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{I}_{\\max }=\\left(\\sqrt{\\mathrm{I}_1}+\\sqrt{\\mathrm{I}_2}\\right)^2 \\\\ & =(\\sqrt{4 \\mathrm{I}}+\\sqrt{9 \\mathrm{I}})^2=25 \\mathrm{I} \\\\ & \\mathrm{I}_{\\min }=\\left(\\sqrt{\\mathrm{I}_1}-\\sqrt{\\mathrm{I}_2}\\right)^2 \\\\ & =(\\sqrt{4 \\mathrm{I}}-\\sqrt{9 \\mathrm{I}})^2=\\mathrm{I} \\\\ & \\mathrm{I}_{\\max }-\\mathrm{I}_{\\min }=24 \\mathrm{I} \\\\ & \\mathrm{x}=24\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}